  "id": "COMPOUND:43208 - PROTEIN:6297",
  "verbalization": "Epothilone C is implicated in the regulation of Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2 through a series of target interactions, with Dipeptidyl peptidase IX acting as a common intermediary. This kinase pathway is supported by multiple independent evidence chains, each linking Epothilone C to a different inhibitor of the target kinase. The consistent presence of Dipeptidyl peptidase IX as a shared target across these pathways suggests a potential mechanism involving the inhibition of a common downstream effector. The overlapping targets indicate that Epothilone C may modulate the activity of the ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2 through a shared regulatory node, possibly by affecting the degradation or activation of this kinase. The robustness of the evidence, combined with the absence of conflicting pathways, supports a mechanistic link between Epothilone C and the ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
